{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening","id":1297283,"title":"Non-humans (especially animals) Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-16T10:13:22-07:00","id":1297283,"title":"Non-humans (especially animals) Awakening","content":"So I know that constructs like golems, clockwork robots, cyborgs, clones, abominations etc can Awaken, as long as they have the intellectual and spiritual capacity (created with both Spirit and Mind 5 I believe).<br /> <br /> Are there situations in which other beings could Awaken? Lupus kinfolk, for example, have a powerful spiritual component and a mind with near or equivalent to human intelligence.<br /> <br /> If you take an animal and &quot;raise&quot; it up using Mind to give it a greater level of intelligence, would that give it the potential to awaken? I ask because an NPC in my chronicle has his wolf half-brother (yes, Garou can have strange families) as his Familiar, and the idea of him Awakening crossed my mind. It almost definitely won't happen but I'm curious about the lore/rules here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:41:42-07:00","id":1297291,"title":"","content":"An uplifted Animal is just another construct, so treated it as such? Historically there were such &quot;noble animals&quot; at least in the history of the world of Darkness.. but they are bygones now. So I would say no on average a Lupus Kinfolk couldn't awaken.. doubly so for a Familiar since that's possessed by a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T07:16:12-07:00","id":1297713,"title":"","content":"Lupus Garou notwithstanding WoD tends to discourage animal splats for some reason. Mundane animals cannot Awaken as per the books, just as they can't be vampires, wraith or changeling.<br /> <br /> Awakened constructs are an exception, not the rule, and mages don't know exactly how they come to be. And all of the canon awakened constructs are humanoid.<br /> <br /> One can theorize that these can be made with Spirit 5, because in Cruzade it's suggested that to &quot;create a human you need Life 5 for the body, Mind 5 for the mind and Spirit 5 <i>for the soul</i>&quot;. Since the soul as opposed to the mind it's always a reference to the Avatar in Mage, one could think that you're granting one. However, this it's a one liner that doesn't explain shit about how the soul works (can an animal have a human soul?) and never get's mentioned again. Avatar <i>creation </i>isn't well established (Keep in mind that if this was possible one could cure Gilgul).<br /> <br /> For all that I would say that the ST has every right to say &quot;only humanoid constructs can have an Avatar&quot; or even &quot;only humanoid constructs <i>with a soul</i> can attract an Avatar&quot;(if you want to make a difference between having a <i>soul </i>and having an Avatar). Or not, maybe the race makes small difference among constructs. Still this certainly lacks precedent and ruling, and thus enters in fiat territory.<br /> <br /> Since wizardly animals ARE part of many real life Traditions I wouldn't see such a fiat with bad eyes. And it doesn't change the setting if it's as rare as other awakened constructs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-18-2019, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T08:17:10-07:00","id":1297726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening?p=1297713#post1297713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all that I would say that the ST has every right to say &quot;only humanoid constructs can have an Avatar&quot; or even &quot;only humanoid constructs <i>with a soul</i> can attract an Avatar&quot;(if you want to make a difference between having a <i>soul </i>and having an Avatar).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would boil it down to &quot;It does not matter what the construct looks like, but to have an avater, the mind has to be essentially human in its ways - for all the extremes that a human mind can go to. But it is human.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" targ