e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T02:03:21-07:00","id":1297907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening?p=1297713#post1297713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lupus Garou notwithstanding WoD tends to discourage animal splats for some reason. Mundane animals cannot Awaken as per the books, just as they can't be vampires, wraith or changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's mostly a matter of lack of pc potential. Animal Breed Fera at least bring animals to human intelligence. An Embraced Pigeon.. would still be a pigeon. A Ghost Cat would.. be very hard to engage with say the themes of WRaith.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Awakened constructs are an exception, not the rule, and mages don't know exactly how they come to be. And all of the canon awakened constructs are humanoid. </div> </div> </div>To be FAIR awakened HUMANS are the exception, not the rule there are a much higher percentage of Awakened Constructs than there are Awakened Humans, even fi the majority of awakened started Human.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One can theorize that these can be made with Spirit 5, because in Cruzade it's suggested that to &quot;create a human you need Life 5 for the body, Mind 5 for the mind and Spirit 5 <i>for the soul</i>&quot;. Since the soul as opposed to the mind it's always a reference to the Avatar in Mage, one could think that you're granting one. However, this it's a one liner that doesn't explain shit about how the soul works (can an animal have a human soul?) and never get's mentioned again. Avatar <i>creation </i>isn't well established (Keep in mind that if this was possible one could cure Gilgul).<br /> <br /> For all that I would say that the ST has every right to say &quot;only humanoid constructs can have an Avatar&quot; or even &quot;only humanoid constructs <i>with a soul</i> can attract an Avatar&quot;(if you want to make a difference between having a <i>soul </i>and having an Avatar). Or not, maybe the race makes small difference among constructs. Still this certainly lacks precedent and ruling, and thus enters in fiat territory.<br /> <br /> Since wizardly animals ARE part of many real life Traditions I wouldn't see such a fiat with bad eyes. And it doesn't change the setting if it's as rare as other awakened constructs </div> </div> </div>I would ultimately make the argument that its probably mechanics that more readily hold back playing a &quot;Noble Animal&quot; A cat doesn't have the same range of traits as a human. IF you uplift them to human intelligence you still ahve to throw a lot of merits at building &quot;A cat&quot; vs a human being. So I'd say that's probably why constructs and wierder mages aren't covered its.. that it requires some rather in depth game shenanigans to pull off and thus backdating why the majority of Mages are normalish people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T04:55:36-07:00","id":1297923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening?p=1297907#post1297907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be FAIR awakened HUMANS are the exception, not the rule there are a much higher percentage of Awakened Constructs than there are Awakened Humans, even fi the majority of awakened started Human.</div> </div> </div> </div>XD that's true. Albeit we don't have exact numbers, it's certain that constructs Awaken more often than humans...if only because constructs are way rarer than humans and yet it isn't unheard off.<br /> <br /> Perhaps being involved in the Awakened world helps one to Awaken...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T05:08:35-07:00","id":1297926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening?p=1297923#post1297923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps being involved in the Awakened world helps one to Awaken...</div> </div> </div> </div> think that's how, fluff-wise, certain nordic and Old Faith fringe groups operate. I mean, just consider the very concept of the Gardeners Of The Tree and their bloodline shenanigans. Now, they themselves might not even know how it works, but seemingly preparing their offspring for a sort of awakening or at least supernatural everyday life seems to *somehow* increase the odds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T06:22:17-07:00","id":1297942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening?p=1297926#post1297926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> think that's how, fluff-wise, certain nordic and Old Faith fringe groups operate. I mean, just consider the very concept of the Gardeners Of The Tree and their bloodline shenanigans. Now, they themselves might not even know how it works, but seemingly preparing their offspring for a sort of awakening or at least supernatural everyday life seems to *somehow* increase the odds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I frame it so that &quot;magical bloodlines&quot;, families of Hermetics and Verbena etc tend to be a mixture of Mages, Sorcerers and Acolytes. Hermetics are very good at initiating Sorcerers and triggering their Awakenings, so some families are full of Mages.<br /> <br /> - Being raised with Magick as a fact of life helps you Awaken, or stops you from falling asleep in the first place.<br /> <br /> - Being raised in an environment rife with magickal/spiritual energies may help you Awaken.<br /> <br /> - Your creation involving magick/magic/splats in some respect will up the odds of you Awakening (constructs, Nephilim and Laham, virgin births via True Faith or Life magick, fae blooded mortals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T08:21:43-07:00","id":1297959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening?p=1297923#post1297923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> XD that's true. Albeit we don't have exact numbers, it's certain that constructs Awaken more often than humans...if only because constructs are way rarer than humans and yet it isn't unheard off.<br /> <br /> Perhaps being involved in the Awakened world helps one to Awaken...</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that a Construct can be explicitly &quot;Built&quot; as incapable of Awakening(the Souless Flaw) this even pushes the point that those with the potential seem to Awaken more readily as every human has a soul(more or less)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T09:20:22-07:00","id":1297973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening?p=1297959#post1297959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that a Construct can be explicitly &quot;Built&quot; as incapable of Awakening(the Souless Flaw) this even pushes the point that those with the potential seem to Awaken more readily as every human has a soul(more or less)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impresion that constructs weren't explicitly built with Flaws, but that these were something that &quot;happened&quot; (albeit the player chooses Flaws to decrease the cost, I don't think the Mage it's calculating these -&quot;mmm, what if I add a Curse to my sword to pay less...&quot;. It doesn't sould very natural)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-19-2019, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T10:55:27-07:00","id":1298006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297283-non-humans-especially-animals-awakening?p=1297973#post1297973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impresion that constructs weren't explicitly built with Flaws, but that these were something that &quot;happened&quot; (albeit the player chooses Flaws to decrease the cost, I don't think the Mage it's calculating these -&quot;mmm, what if I add a Curse to my sword to pay less...&quot;. It doesn't sould very natural)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't mean it as an explicit point of choice. Just that Of the Constructs made those who have a chance at success have a higher chance on a percentage as there aren't any Souless humans(not counting some really fucked up statements in Progenitors 1e). I don't think Construct.. ing? Is well enough understood to control this currently though.<br /> <br /> Now as for Flaws on magic items.. I'd say it depends in general? &quot;I'm making this evil sword require virgin blood every month to function&quot; is probably a intentional flaw built by the builder because he's an evil bastard? Though it could just as readily be driven by their incompitence as a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T11:15:22-07:00","id":1298012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't mean it as an explicit point of choice. Just that Of the Constructs made those who have a chance at success have a higher chance on a percentage as there aren't any Souless humans(not counting some really fucked up statements in Progenitors 1e). I don't think Construct.. ing? Is well enough understood to control this currently though.</div> </div> </div> </div>O yes, it does add to your point. It's said that such that Flaw it's common in constructs. Depending on how common it may increase the percentage a lot or a little, but it's always an increase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now as for Flaws on magic items.. I'd say it depends in general? &quot;I'm making this evil sword require virgin blood every month to function&quot; is probably a intentional flaw built by the builder because he's an evil bastard? Though it could just as readily be driven by their incompitence as a mage. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're right. The mechanic could be used to represent both things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}